{"name":"Aquamarine Dream","hex":"#b3c4ba","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"aquamarine","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The bluish-green colour of the sea.","A transparent bluish-green, sometimes yellow-green, variety of beryl."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a bluish-green colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aquamarine"},{"term":"dream","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Imaginary events seen in the mind while sleeping.","A hope or wish."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To see imaginary events in one's mind while sleeping.","To hope, to wish."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dream"}],"entries":[{"title":"Aquamarine (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Aquamarine is a 2006 American teen fantasy romantic comedy film directed by Elizabeth Allen, loosely based on the 2001 young adult novel of the same name by Alice Hoffman."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/74/Aquamarine_%28poster%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aquamarine_(film)","wikidata":"Q623072"},{"title":"Aquamarine (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Aquamarine\" is a song by American singer Addison Rae. It was released on October 25, 2024, through Columbia Records, as the second single from Rae's debut studio album, Addison. Just like its predecessor, the song received praise from critics and wider audiences. The deep house and dance-pop song with strong Eurodance influences' lyrics speak about self-discovery. The song was co-written by Addison Rae, Elvira Anderfjärd and Luka Kloser. An accompanying music video was directed by Sean Price Williams and filmed in Paris, France. It received a nomination for Best Newcomer Pop/R&B/Soul/Jazz Video at the 2025 UK Music Video Awards."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1d/Addison_Rae_-_Aquamarine.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aquamarine_(song)","wikidata":"Q130640565"},{"title":"Dream","blocks":[{"text":"A dream is a succession of images, dynamic scenes and situations, ideas, emotions, and sensations that usually occur involuntarily in the mind during certain stages of sleep. Humans generally spend more than two hours dreaming per night, and each dream lasts around 5–20 minutes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/A_dream_%28BM_1868%2C0808.9057%29.jpg/330px-A_dream_%28BM_1868%2C0808.9057%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dream","wikidata":"Q36348"},{"title":"Aquamarine (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Aquamarine is a pale blue-green color between cyan and cerulean on the color wheel. It is named after the mineral aquamarine, a gemstone mainly found in granite rocks. The first recorded use of aquamarine as a color name in English was in 1598."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/2a/Aquamarine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aquamarine_(color)","wikidata":"Q372973"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/46/Arca_Addison_Rae_Aquamarine_remix_cover.jpg/250px-Arca_Addison_Rae_Aquamarine_remix_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/46/Arca_Addison_Rae_Aquamarine_remix_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/46/Arca_Addison_Rae_Aquamarine_remix_cover.jpg/250px-Arca_Addison_Rae_Aquamarine_remix_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AArca_Addison_Rae_Aquamarine_remix_cover.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wi